---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { recruitment } from '../data/content';
import { positionsLabel, recruitmentStatusLabel } from '../lib/content';

const interests = [
  'Floating offshore wind structures: moorings, dynamic power cables, virtual sensing, and digital twins',
  'Structural integrity and fracture mechanics: ultimate strength, engineering critical assessment, impact and crashworthiness',
  'Scientific software development for marine structures: state estimation, surrogate modelling, differentiable simulation',
  'Green marine infrastructure: fracture assessment of hydrogen and ammonia containment systems (emerging direction)',
];
---

<Base
  title="Join us"
  description="Graduate positions in the SMI Lab: research on floating offshore wind structural integrity, built into open-source software."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Opportunities"
    title="Build the tools the offshore wind industry doesn't have yet"
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <p class="ko">
        함께 연구할 대학원생을 모집하고 있습니다. 관심 있는 인하대 조선해양공학과 학부생은
        메일로 연락한 후 면담 바랍니다:{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>

      <p>
        Graduate students in this lab do two things at once. They carry out research on the
        structural integrity of floating offshore wind systems, and they build that research
        into software using the practices of professional engineering teams: Git,
        automated testing, continuous integration, documentation, and AI-assisted development
        with tools such as Claude Code. By the time they graduate, students here will have
        journal publications and a public software portfolio—a combination that few graduate
        programmes in this field offer.
      </p>

      <h2>Areas we are recruiting in</h2>
      <ul>
        {interests.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>Visiting researchers</h2>
      <p>
        We host visiting researchers and exchange students for defined periods of joint work.
        Please write with your research interests, the period you have in mind, and any
        funding you already hold.
      </p>

      <h2>Industry collaboration</h2>
      <p>
        We work with classification societies, offshore wind developers, shipyards, and
        technology developers on mooring and cable integrity, structural assessment, fatigue
        and fracture, and alternative fuel containment. Collaboration ranges from focused
        technical studies to multi-year funded projects.
      </p>

      <h2>How to get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Email{' '}<a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with a short description
        of your interests. For graduate applications, please include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>A CV, including your academic record</li>
        <li>A brief statement of the research problems that interest you and why</li>
        <li>Your intended start date and funding situation, if known</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Open positions</h2>
      {
        recruitment.active ? (
          <div class="open-positions">
            <p class="eyebrow">{recruitmentStatusLabel()}</p>
            <p><strong>{positionsLabel()}</strong> are available for the {recruitment.intake}.</p>
            <p class="muted">
              Undergraduate research slots are {recruitment.undergraduateSlotsAvailable
                ? 'also available.'
                : 'currently full.'}
            </p>
            {!recruitment.openUntil && (
              <p class="muted">
                No closing date has been published. Please contact us for the current
                application timetable.
              </p>
            )}
          </div>
        ) : (
          <p>There are no open graduate positions at present.</p>
        )
      }

      <h2>What we look for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          An undergraduate GPA of 3.50 or above in Naval Architecture and Ocean Engineering.
          Engineers from related fields may also qualify.
        </li>
        <li>Competence in at least one programming language, for example Python or C++.</li>
        <li>Familiarity with finite element analysis concepts.</li>
        <li>
          Prior involvement in relevant work strengthens an application: capstone design,
          research internships, or CAE competitions such as the KSOE competition.
        </li>
        <li>
          Experience with AI-assisted development tools such as Claude Code is an advantage.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we expect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Independent investigation using computational tools such as Abaqus and OrcaFlex.
        </li>
        <li>Completion of the thesis within two years.</li>
        <li>
          At least one publication in a domestic or international journal or conference
          proceedings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="evidence">
        This training is demonstrated in practice: the lab's packages are available through the{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/SMI-Lab-Inha">SMI-Lab-Inha GitHub organisation</a>, and
        the public packages show the standard of work expected from students.
      </p>

      <h2>What we provide</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A full research assistantship, including tuition support and a monthly stipend.</li>
        <li>Access to lab computing resources.</li>
        <li>Conference funding.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .ko {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent);
    background: var(--c-bg-subtle);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .evidence {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-sky);
    background: var(--c-accent-soft);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }

  .open-positions {
    border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    background: var(--c-bg-subtle);
  }

  .open-positions p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .pending-block {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--c-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--c-bg-subtle);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pending-block p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
